WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:05.600
168 years before Game of Thrones, the Targaryens
were at their peak in Westeros.

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:09.530
There were many Targaryens and even more dragons.

00:00:09.530 --> 00:00:14.320
From the perspective of every house in the
Seven Kingdoms (major or minor) as well as

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:19.750
from the perspective of commoners and even
from the perspective of the Targaryens themselves,

00:00:19.750 --> 00:00:25.460
the Targaryen rule seemed to be so powerful
that even 1000 years from then on, they would

00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:29.840
still rule the continent, but then the Dance
of the Dragons happened.

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:35.239
It was a Targaryen civil war that saw the
end of many Targaryens and most of their dragons.

00:00:35.239 --> 00:00:38.239
It nearly destroyed their entire house.

00:00:38.239 --> 00:00:42.730
This is one of the most exciting and most
epic events that ever happened in the history

00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:47.280
of this world and it’s exactly the event
that House of the Dragon will follow.

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:51.149
Therefore it shouldn’t come as a surprise
that many main characters of the show are

00:00:51.149 --> 00:00:55.969
going to be the dragon-lord ancestors of Daenerys
Targaryen and Jon Snow.

00:00:55.969 --> 00:01:00.609
The series is based on George R.R. Martin’s
book Fire And Blood which covers the entire

00:01:00.609 --> 00:01:06.270
Targaryen history in Westeros, starting from
Aegon Targaryen and his conquest, and going

00:01:06.270 --> 00:01:11.430
to the Dance of the Dragons while Fire And
Blood part 2 will also cover the Blackfyre

00:01:11.430 --> 00:01:15.190
Rebellions and will end with Robert’s Rebellion.

00:01:15.190 --> 00:01:19.860
The prequel series House of the Dragon finds
the Targaryen dynasty at the absolute apex

00:01:19.860 --> 00:01:25.030
of its power, with around 20 dragons flying
over King’s Landing and Dragonstone.

00:01:25.030 --> 00:01:29.320
Most empires—real and imagined—crumble
from such heights.

00:01:29.320 --> 00:01:35.340
In the case of the Targaryens, their slow
fall begins almost 192 years before the events

00:01:35.340 --> 00:01:40.870
of Game of Thrones, when King Viserys Targaryen
breaks with a century of tradition by naming

00:01:40.870 --> 00:01:43.680
his daughter Rhaenyra heir to the Iron Throne.

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:48.900
But when Viserys later fathers a son, the
court is shocked that Rhaenyra retains her

00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:53.820
status as his heir, and seeds of division
sow friction across the realm.

00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:59.440
So, basically, the show starts with King Viserys
I Targaryen sitting on the Iron Throne with

00:01:59.440 --> 00:02:05.270
Rhaenyra, his oldest child, being his heir
instead of his son Aegon, much to displeasure

00:02:05.270 --> 00:02:07.590
of Aegon’s mother Queen Alicent Hightower.

00:02:07.590 --> 00:02:12.499
Through a series of flashbacks, we will learn
about why King Viserys chose to keep Rhaenyra

00:02:12.499 --> 00:02:15.890
as his designated heir even when he got a
son.

00:02:15.890 --> 00:02:20.540
We’ll also learn about the tension in the
King’s Landing court between Rhaenyra’s

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:25.249
faction and Alicent’s faction, or in the
other words, between the Blacks and the Greens.

00:02:25.249 --> 00:02:30.739
Rhaenyra’s faction obviously supports Rhaenyra
while Alicent’s faction supports Aegon as

00:02:30.739 --> 00:02:33.280
the future ruler of Westeros.

00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:38.950
King Viserys I Targaryen had three children
by his first queen, Aemma Arryn, but only

00:02:38.950 --> 00:02:42.239
one, Princess Rhaenyra, survived to adulthood.

00:02:42.239 --> 00:02:47.609
Lacking a son to succeed him, Viserys began
to train Rhaenyra to be his heir.

00:02:47.609 --> 00:02:52.230
Young Rhaenyra was included in discussions
of the affairs of the state and was allowed

00:02:52.230 --> 00:02:55.660
to participate in meetings of the small council.

00:02:55.660 --> 00:03:01.340
Many of the nobles took note, and Rhaenyra
soon acquired a huge number of supporters.

00:03:01.340 --> 00:03:06.140
After the passing of Queen Aemma, Viserys
named Rhaenyra his heir, and hundreds of lords

00:03:06.140 --> 00:03:09.230
and landed knights paid obeisance to her.

00:03:09.230 --> 00:03:14.750
The king later remarried to Alicent Hightower
and had four more children: Aegon, Helaena,

00:03:14.750 --> 00:03:16.400
Aemond, and Daeron.

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:21.159
A great tourney was held at King's Landing
on the fifth anniversary of Viserys's marriage

00:03:21.159 --> 00:03:22.719
to Alicent.

00:03:22.719 --> 00:03:28.150
During the opening feast, Queen Alicent wore
a green gown, while Princess Rhaenyra dressed

00:03:28.150 --> 00:03:31.020
in the red and black of House Targaryen.

00:03:31.020 --> 00:03:35.249
Note was taken, and thereafter it became the
custom to refer to "greens" and "blacks" when

00:03:35.249 --> 00:03:38.870
talking of the queen's party and the party
of the princess, respectively.

00:03:38.870 --> 00:03:43.700
While many expected that the King would change
the succession order and the Hightowers tried

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:48.860
to persuade him to do so many times, Viserys
only strengthened Rhaenyra's place in the

00:03:48.860 --> 00:03:55.010
succession by marrying her to Ser Laenor Velaryon
- who himself had Targaryen blood through

00:03:55.010 --> 00:03:57.209
his mother, Princess Rhaenys.

00:03:57.209 --> 00:04:02.629
It’s not a big spoiler as his character
is not that important, but in season 1 Laenor

00:04:02.629 --> 00:04:07.809
will be executed (but I won’t tell you by
who although you will probably figure it out)

00:04:07.809 --> 00:04:13.090
and after Rhaenyra’s husband gets executed,
Rhaenyra will marry her uncle, Prince Daemon

00:04:13.090 --> 00:04:15.590
Targaryen, younger brother to Viserys.

00:04:15.590 --> 00:04:22.310
This only strengthens her position even more
as Daemon himself has a lot of supporters

00:04:22.310 --> 00:04:26.730
and is arguably the best warrior, commander,
and general of this time.

00:04:26.730 --> 00:04:31.210
In season 1 it will also be established that
Alicent’s and Rhaenyra’s children have

00:04:31.210 --> 00:04:36.300
hatred towards each other, which will lead
to many horrible events by the time the war

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:37.370
breaks out.

00:04:37.370 --> 00:04:43.220
Speaking of the war breaking out, things start
to escalate towards the end of season 1.

00:04:43.220 --> 00:04:48.780
King Viserys dies, Queen Alicent Hightower
conceals Viserys's death from the public and

00:04:48.780 --> 00:04:53.889
instead has Ser Criston Cole, Lord Commander
of the Kingsguard, summon the small council

00:04:53.889 --> 00:04:57.180
to Alicent's apartments in Maegor's Holdfast.

00:04:57.180 --> 00:05:02.370
Grand Maester Orwyle here predicts a war,
believing that Rhaenya would never be willing

00:05:02.370 --> 00:05:06.370
to give up her birthright, and had dragons
at her disposal.

00:05:06.370 --> 00:05:11.450
When Lyman declares that he was not willing
to listen to people plotting to steal Rhaenyra’s

00:05:11.450 --> 00:05:15.210
crown and attempts to leave, Ser Criston kills
him.

00:05:15.210 --> 00:05:19.560
This makes Lyman the first casualty of the
Dance of the Dragons.

00:05:19.560 --> 00:05:24.520
After Lyman's death, the green council made
their plans, vowing their loyalty to their

00:05:24.520 --> 00:05:29.979
new king, and arresting all those in King's
Landing who could be loyal to Rhaenyra.

00:05:29.979 --> 00:05:33.370
To all those who might be loyal to Aegon,
ravens are sent.

00:05:33.370 --> 00:05:38.730
Prince Aemond (Aegon’s brother) is sent
to Storm's End to betroth himself to one of

00:05:38.730 --> 00:05:43.840
Lord Borros Baratheon's daughters, so House
Baratheon might fight for Aegon II.

00:05:43.840 --> 00:05:49.310
Meanwhile, Rhaenyra remains on Dragonstone,
unaware of what happened instead of coming

00:05:49.310 --> 00:05:51.659
to King’s Landing to claim the throne.

00:05:51.659 --> 00:05:56.870
Criston who once served Rhaenyra, convinced
Viserys's son, Prince Aegon the Elder, to

00:05:56.870 --> 00:06:00.240
claim the rule of the Seven Kingdoms as his
father lay dead.

00:06:00.240 --> 00:06:03.480
For this, he became known as Criston the Kingmaker.

00:06:03.480 --> 00:06:08.879
Viserys had decreed his heir to be Rhaenyra
Targaryen, Princess of Dragonstone, the daughter

00:06:08.879 --> 00:06:11.470
from his first wife, Aemma Arryn.

00:06:11.470 --> 00:06:17.060
The greens at the Red Keep support Aegon the
Elder, the eldest son of his second wife Alicent,

00:06:17.060 --> 00:06:22.370
however, and Criston takes into custody any
blacks remaining at court.

00:06:22.370 --> 00:06:26.479
Alicent forbids septons and silent sisters
from treating Viserys's body.

00:06:26.479 --> 00:06:32.360
A week after Viserys's death, his passing
is finally publicly revealed with the greens

00:06:32.360 --> 00:06:35.830
accounting the accession of Aegon II Targaryen.

00:06:35.830 --> 00:06:41.970
The silent sisters then prepare the late king's
body for the traditional burning of a Targaryen.

00:06:41.970 --> 00:06:44.509
Aegon's coronation is hastily prepared.

00:06:44.509 --> 00:06:50.530
The Dragonpit is chosen as the site for its
towering bronze doors, strong roof, and thick

00:06:50.530 --> 00:06:53.409
walls making it easily defensible.

00:06:53.409 --> 00:06:59.280
Ser Criston Cole crowns Aegon, while Alicent
Hightower crowns Aegon's sister-wife, Helaena.

00:06:59.280 --> 00:07:04.039
However, the night before, the first defection
had taken place.

00:07:04.039 --> 00:07:08.469
Ser Steffon Darklyn of the Kingsguard had
left the city, with, amongst other things,

00:07:08.469 --> 00:07:15.639
the crown worn by kings, Jaehaerys I and Viserys
I and is taking it to the rightful Queen Rhaenyra.

00:07:15.639 --> 00:07:21.689
At Dragonstone, Rhaenyra finds out that her
father died and Aegon staged a coup and was

00:07:21.689 --> 00:07:24.080
crowned King in King’s Landing.

00:07:24.080 --> 00:07:29.120
Furious, Rhaenyra quickly made her own council
at Dragonstone, the black council.

00:07:29.120 --> 00:07:34.599
The participants are, amongst others, her
uncle-husband Daemon, her three eldest sons

00:07:34.599 --> 00:07:41.130
Jacaerys, Lucerys, and Joffrey, Lord Corlys
Velaryon, and his wife, Princess Rhaenys.

00:07:41.130 --> 00:07:46.409
Rhaenyra is crowned queen, using the crown
her father and great-grandfather had worn,

00:07:46.409 --> 00:07:51.430
thanks to Ser Steffon Darklyn, who had arrived
from King's Landing.

00:07:51.430 --> 00:07:56.759
Prince Daemon places the crown on Rhaenyra's
head himself and is named the Protector of

00:07:56.759 --> 00:08:01.949
the Realm, and Jacaerys is officially named
Prince of Dragonstone and heir to the Iron

00:08:01.949 --> 00:08:02.949
Throne.

00:08:02.949 --> 00:08:07.370
During the council it’s resolved that while
Rhaenyra remains at Dragonstone to regain

00:08:07.370 --> 00:08:12.729
her health, Prince Daemon and Caraxes would
travel to the Riverlands, to make Harrenhal

00:08:12.729 --> 00:08:16.659
their base and rallying point for those loyal
to Rhaenyra.

00:08:16.659 --> 00:08:21.689
House Velaryon would close off the Gullet
blocking all shipping from Blackwater Bay.

00:08:21.689 --> 00:08:26.389
Princess Rhaenys is convinced that Storm's
End would declare for Rhaenyra, since Lord

00:08:26.389 --> 00:08:31.449
Boremund Baratheon, the deceased father of
Lord Borros and Rhaenys's uncle, had always

00:08:31.449 --> 00:08:34.000
been a supporter of Rhaenys.

00:08:34.000 --> 00:08:38.620
Prince Daemon is also convinced that Lady
Jeyne Arryn, the Maiden of the Vale, would

00:08:38.620 --> 00:08:43.850
bring her support to their side as Rhaenyra’s
mother was Arryn herself.

00:08:43.850 --> 00:08:48.750
Although they believe the North to be too
remote to play an important part in the war,

00:08:48.750 --> 00:08:54.380
messages are to be sent to those lords nevertheless,
with the eldest Jacaerys visiting the Arryns

00:08:54.380 --> 00:08:58.970
of the Eyrie, the Manderlys of White Harbor,
and the Starks of Winterfell.

00:08:58.970 --> 00:09:03.230
Rhaenyra's second son, Lucerys, travels to
Storm's End.

00:09:03.230 --> 00:09:07.550
Rhaenyra proclaims King Aegon and his mother
Queen Alicent as well as all their supporters

00:09:07.550 --> 00:09:10.610
– traitors and enemy of house Targaryen.

00:09:10.610 --> 00:09:15.790
Back at King's Landing, at this point already
a King, Aegon proclaims Rhaenyra traitor and

00:09:15.790 --> 00:09:20.370
the enemy of House Targaryen, and thus the
Targaryen civil war starts.

00:09:20.370 --> 00:09:27.420
Dragons will dance, swords will clash, monarchs
will rise and fall, and season 1 will end,

00:09:27.420 --> 00:09:31.510
leaving you to impatiently wait for season
2 to see what happens next.

00:09:31.510 --> 00:09:36.590
Basically, The House of the Dragon is focused
on the war of succession between Aegon II

00:09:36.590 --> 00:09:42.350
and his half-sister Rhaenyra over their father
Viserys I's throne, the war that will be fought

00:09:42.350 --> 00:09:45.510
from 129 AC to 131 AC.

00:09:45.510 --> 00:09:50.160
It will see the deaths of monarchs, the deaths
of Targaryens and their dragons as well as

00:09:50.160 --> 00:09:54.380
major battles across the Seven Kingdoms with
the Starks and the Velaryons fighting the

00:09:54.380 --> 00:09:59.740
hardest on Rhaenryra’s side and the Lannisters
and Baratheons fighting the hardest on Aegon’s

00:09:59.740 --> 00:10:00.740
side.

00:10:00.740 --> 00:10:03.470
All of this and more you will see in 2022
on HBO.

00:10:03.470 --> 00:10:07.440
Thank you so much for watching, if you enjoyed
this video please give it a big thumbs up

00:10:07.440 --> 00:10:14.810
and I hope to see you in the next one, peace!

